zeros of theta_QNR among alpha^e: e in [3, 5, 6]
zeros of theta_QR  among alpha^e: e in [1, 2, 4]
[PASS] (3) WHICH CODE: theta_QNR vanishes exactly on the NONRESIDUE powers of alpha  =>  <theta_QNR> = N = <n(x)>, dim (p+1)/2
[PASS] (3) control: theta_QR vanishes exactly on the RESIDUE powers  =>  <theta_QR> = Q = <q(x)>
[PASS] (3) divisibility cross-check: n(x) | theta_QNR and q(x) !| theta_QNR
Gauss periods: eta_R = 0, eta_N = 1 (in GF(2^3); eta_R + eta_N must be 1)
